<http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Line_Cinema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**New Line Cinema** is an American [film production](:Film_production) studio owned by [Warner Bros. Discovery](:Warner_Bros%2E_Discovery) and is a film label of [Warner Bros](:Warner_Bros%2E). It was founded in 1967 by [Robert Shaye](:Robert_Shaye) as an independent film distribution company; later becoming a film studio. It was acquired by [Turner Broadcasting System](:Turner_Broadcasting_System) in 1994; Turner later merged with Time Warner (later known as [WarnerMedia](:WarnerMedia) from 2018 to 2022) in 1996, and New Line was merged with [Warner Bros. Pictures](:Warner_Bros%2E_Pictures) in 2008. The studio has been nicknamed, \"The House that [Freddy](:Freddy_Krueger) Built\" due to the success of the *[Nightmare on Elm Street](:A_Nightmare_on_Elm_Street_%28franchise%29)* film series."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
