<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bernice_Hansen> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Berneice Edna Hansell (July 11, 1897 – April 16, 1981), known as Bernice Hansen, was an American voice actress. She was best known for providing the voices for both female and young male characters in the mid to late 1930s for various cartoon studios, most notably Warner Bros. Cartoons, where she played Little Kitty in I Haven't Got a Hat (1935)."@en .
