<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Friz_Freleng> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Isadore** \"**Friz**\" **Freleng** (August 21, 1905 – May 26, 1995), credited as **I. Freleng** early in his career, was an American [animator](:Animator), [cartoonist](:Cartoonist), [director](:Film_director), [producer](:Film_producer), and [composer](:Composer) known for his work at [Warner Bros. Cartoons](:Warner_Bros%2E_Cartoons) on the *[Looney Tunes](:Looney_Tunes)* and *[Merrie Melodies](:Merrie_Melodies)* series of [cartoons](:Cartoon). In total he created more than 300 cartoons.He introduced and/or developed several of the studio's biggest stars, including [Bugs Bunny](:Bugs_Bunny), [Porky Pig](:Porky_Pig), [Tweety](:Tweety), [Sylvester](:Sylvester_the_Cat), [Yosemite Sam](:Yosemite_Sam) (to whom he was said to bear more than a passing resemblance), and [Speedy Gonzales](:Speedy_Gonzales). The senior director at Warners' [Termite Terrace](:Termite_Terrace) studio, Freleng directed more cartoons than any other director in the studio (a total of 266), and is also the most honored of the Warner directors, having won five [Academy Awards](:Academy_Awards) and three [Emmy Awards](:Emmy_Awards). After Warner closed down the animation studio in 1963, Freleng and business partner [David H. DePatie](:David_H%2E_DePatie) founded [DePatie–Freleng Enterprises](:DePatie%E2%80%93Freleng_Enterprises), which produced cartoons (including *[The Pink Panther Show](:The_Pink_Panther_Show)*), feature film title sequences, and [Saturday-morning cartoons](:Saturday-morning_cartoon) through the early 1980s.The nickname \"Friz\" came from his friend, [Hugh Harman](:Hugh_Harman), who initially nicknamed him \"Congressman Frizby\" after a fictional senator who appeared in [satirical](:Satire) pieces in the *[Los Angeles Examiner](:Los_Angeles_Examiner)*, due to the characters strong resemblance to him. Over time, this shortened to \"Friz\"."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
