<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jesse_Plemons> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Jesse Plemons** (; born April 2, 1988) is an American actor. He began his career as a child actor and achieved a career breakthrough with his major role as [Landry Clarke](:List_of_Friday_Night_Lights_characters) in the [NBC](:NBC) drama series *[Friday Night Lights](:Friday_Night_Lights_%28TV_series%29)* (2006–2011). He subsequently portrayed [Todd Alquist](:List_of_characters_in_the_Breaking_Bad_franchise%23Todd_Alquist) in [season 5](:Breaking_Bad_%28season_5%29) of the [AMC](:AMC_%28TV_channel%29) crime drama series *[Breaking Bad](:Breaking_Bad)* (2012–2013) and its sequel film *[El Camino: A Breaking Bad Movie](:El_Camino%3A_A_Breaking_Bad_Movie)* (2019). For his role as [Ed Blumquist](:Ed_Blumquist) in [season 2](:Fargo_%28season_2%29) of the [FX](:FX_%28TV_channel%29) anthology series *[Fargo](:Fargo_%28TV_series%29)* (2015), he received his first [Primetime Emmy Award](:Primetime_Emmy_Award) nomination and won a [Critics' Choice Television Award](:Critics%27_Choice_Television_Award). He received a second Emmy nomination for his portrayal of Robert Daly in \"[USS Callister](:USS_Callister)\", an episode of the [Netflix](:Netflix) anthology series *[Black Mirror](:Black_Mirror)* (2017).Plemons has appeared in supporting roles in several films including *[The Master](:The_Master_%282012_film%29)* (2012), *[The Homesman](:The_Homesman)* (2014), *[Black Mass](:Black_Mass_%28film%29)*, *[Bridge of Spies](:Bridge_of_Spies_%28film%29)* (both 2015), *[Game Night](:Game_Night_%28film%29)*, *[Vice](:Vice_%282018_film%29)* (both 2018), *[The Irishman](:The_Irishman_%282019_film%29)* (2019), *[Judas and the Black Messiah](:Judas_and_the_Black_Messiah)*, *[Jungle Cruise](:Jungle_Cruise_%28film%29)*, and *[The Power of the Dog](:The_Power_of_the_Dog_%28film%29)* (all in 2021). He starred in the psychological thriller film *[I'm Thinking of Ending Things](:I%27m_Thinking_of_Ending_Things_%28film%29)* (2020). He was nominated for the [Independent Spirit Award for Best Male Lead](:Independent_Spirit_Award_for_Best_Male_Lead) for his role as David Mulcahey in *[Other People](:Other_People_%28film%29)* (2016). For his performance in *[The Power of the Dog](:The_Power_of_the_Dog_%28film%29)*, he was nominated for a [BAFTA Award for Best Actor in a Supporting Role](:BAFTA_Award_for_Best_Actor_in_a_Supporting_Role) and the [Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor](:Academy_Award_for_Best_Supporting_Actor)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
