<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bernard_Durning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bernard Joseph Durning (August 24, 1893 – August 29, 1923) was an American silent film director and actor who worked primarily with Lon Chaney, Dustin Farnum, and Buck Jones. William A. Wellman was his assistant director and protégé. His older brother, Harry M. Durning, was the Collector of Customs for the Port of New York from 1933 to 1953."@en .
