<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Christopher_Plummer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Arthur Christopher Orme Plummer** [CC](:Order_of_Canada) (December 13, 1929 – February 5, 2021) was a Canadian actor. His career spanned 65 years, gaining him recognition for his performances in film, stage, and television. He received [multiple accolades](:List_of_awards_and_nominations_received_by_Christopher_Plummer), including an [Academy Award](:Academy_Award), two [Tony Awards](:Tony_Awards), two [Primetime Emmy Awards](:Primetime_Emmy_Awards) and a [Grammy Award](:Grammy_Award) nomination―making him the only Canadian recipient of the \"[Triple Crown of Acting](:Triple_Crown_of_Acting)\" to [also acquire a Grammy nomination](:List_of_EGOT_winners%23Missing_a_Grammy_Award). He made his Broadway debut in 1954 and continued to act in leading roles on stage, playing [Cyrano de Bergerac](:Cyrano_de_Bergerac) in *[Cyrano](:Cyrano_%28musical%29)* (1974), [Iago](:Iago) in *[Othello](:Othello)*, as well as playing the titular roles in *[Hamlet at Elsinore](:Hamlet_at_Elsinore)* (1964), *[Macbeth](:Macbeth)*, *[King Lear](:King_Lear)*, and *[Barrymore](:Barrymore_%28play%29)*. Plummer performed in stage productions, including *[J.B.](:J%2EB%2E_%28play%29)*, *[No Man's Land](:No_Man%27s_Land_%28play%29)*, and *[Inherit the Wind](:Inherit_the_Wind_%28play%29)*.Plummer was born in [Toronto, Ontario](:Toronto%2C_Ontario), and grew up in [Senneville, Quebec](:Senneville%2C_Quebec), a suburb of [Montreal](:Montreal). After appearing on stage, he made his film debut in *[Stage Struck](:Stage_Struck_%281958_film%29)* (1958), landed his first starring role that same year in *[Wind Across the Everglades](:Wind_Across_the_Everglades)*, and won widespread acclaim for his performance as Captain [Georg von Trapp](:Georg_von_Trapp) in the [musical film](:Musical_film) *[The Sound of Music](:The_Sound_of_Music_%28film%29)* (1965) alongside [Julie Andrews](:Julie_Andrews).Plummer played numerous major historical figures, including [Commodus](:Commodus) in *[The Fall of the Roman Empire](:The_Fall_of_the_Roman_Empire_%28film%29)* (1964), [Arthur Wellesley, 1st Duke of Wellington](:Arthur_Wellesley%2C_1st_Duke_of_Wellington) in *[Waterloo](:Waterloo_%281970_film%29)* (1970), [Rudyard Kipling](:Rudyard_Kipling) in *[The Man Who Would Be King](:The_Man_Who_Would_Be_King_%28film%29)* (1975), [Mike Wallace](:Mike_Wallace) in *[The Insider](:The_Insider_%28film%29)* (1999), [Leo Tolstoy](:Leo_Tolstoy) in *[The Last Station](:The_Last_Station)* (2009), [Kaiser Wilhelm II](:Kaiser_Wilhelm_II) in *[The Exception](:The_Exception)* (2016), and [J. Paul Getty](:J%2E_Paul_Getty) in *[All the Money in the World](:All_the_Money_in_the_World)* (2017). His film credits also include *[Malcolm X](:Malcolm_X_%281992_film%29)* (1992), *[A Beautiful Mind](:A_Beautiful_Mind_%28film%29)* (2001), *[The New World](:The_New_World_%282005_film%29)* (2005), *[Inside Man](:Inside_Man)* (2006), *[The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo](:The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_%282011_film%29)* (2011), *[Knives Out](:Knives_Out)* (2019), and *[The Last Full Measure](:The_Last_Full_Measure_%282019_film%29)* (2019).Plummer received various awards for his work, including an [Academy Award](:Academy_Awards), two [Primetime Emmy Awards](:Primetime_Emmy_Award), two [Tony Awards](:Tony_Award), a [Golden Globe Award](:Golden_Globe_Award), a [Screen Actors Guild Award](:Screen_Actors_Guild_Award), and a [British Academy Film Award](:British_Academy_Film_Awards). He is one of the few performers to have received the [Triple Crown of Acting](:Triple_Crown_of_Acting), and the only Canadian to accomplish this feat. In 2011, he won the [Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor](:Academy_Award_for_Best_Supporting_Actor) at the age of 82 for *[Beginners](:Beginners)* (2010), becoming the oldest person to win an acting award from the [Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences](:Academy_of_Motion_Picture_Arts_and_Sciences) (a distinction he held until being supplanted by 83-year-old [Anthony Hopkins](:Anthony_Hopkins) in 2021), and he also received an Oscar nomination at the age of 88 for *All the Money in the World*, making him the oldest person to be nominated in any acting category at the Academy Awards."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
