<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pathé> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Pathé** or **Pathé Frères** (Template:IPA-fr, styled as **PATHÉ!**) is the name of various [French](:French_people) [businesses](:Business) that were founded and originally run by the Pathé Brothers of [France](:France) starting in 1896. In the early 1900s, Pathé became the world's largest film equipment and production company, as well as a major producer of [phonograph records](:Phonograph_record). In 1908, Pathé invented the [newsreel](:Newsreel) that was shown in cinemas before a feature film.Pathé is a major film production and distribution company, owning a number of cinema chains through its subsidiary [Les Cinémas Pathé Gaumont](:Les_Cin%C3%A9mas_Path%C3%A9_Gaumont) and television networks across Europe. It is the second-oldest operating film company behind [Gaumont Film Company](:Gaumont_Film_Company), which was established in 1895."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
