<http://dbpedia.org/resource/José_Salcedo_(film_editor)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**José Salcedo Palomeque** (c. 1949 – 19 September 2017) was a Spanish film editor with over 120 feature film credits. He had an extended collaboration with the director [Pedro Almodóvar](:Pedro_Almod%C3%B3var), having edited all of Almodóvar's films from 1980 until his death.Salcedo had been nominated many times for [Goya Award for Best Editing](:Goya_Award_for_Best_Editing), and won the award three times: for *[Women on the Verge of a Nervous Breakdown](:Women_on_the_Verge_of_a_Nervous_Breakdown)* ([1988](:3rd_Goya_Awards%29), *[Nobody Will Speak of Us When We're Dead](:Nobody_Will_Speak_of_Us_When_We%27re_Dead)* ([1995](:10th_Goya_Awards%29), and *[All About My Mother](:All_About_My_Mother)* ([1999](:14th_Goya_Awards%29). He was honored with the 2017 [Gold Medal](https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academia%20de%20las%20Artes%20y%20las%20Ciencias%20Cinematográficas%20de%20España#Medalla_de_Oro_de_la_Academia_de_las_Artes_y_las_Ciencias_Cinematográficas_de_España) of the *[Academia de las Artes y las Ciencias Cinematográficas de España](:Academia_de_las_Artes_y_las_Ciencias_Cinematogr%C3%A1ficas_de_Espa%C3%B1a)*, which is the Spanish academy that awards the Goyas."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
