<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Charles_R._Macauley> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Charles Raymond \"C. R.\" Macauley (March 19, 1871 – November 24, 1934) was an American cartoonist and illustrator. He was also involved in the film business. Born in Canton, Ohio, he worked as a freelance illustrator and as staff cartoonist for newspapers including the Cleveland World, New York World, New York Daily Mirror, New York Evening Graphic, and Brooklyn Daily Eagle. He received the 1930 Pulitzer Prize for Editorial Cartooning for his 1929 cartoon \"Paying for a Dead Horse\". \n* Cartoon depicting the profits of child labor, c. 1913 \n* 1917 Liberty bond poster \n* \"Paying for a Dead Horse\", 1929"@en .
