<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Susan_Penhaligon> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Susan Penhaligon** (born 3 July 1949) is a British actress and writer known for her role in the drama series *[Bouquet of Barbed Wire](:Bouquet_of_Barbed_Wire)* (1976), and for playing Helen Barker in the sitcom *[A Fine Romance](:A_Fine_Romance_%281981_TV_series%29)* (1981–1984).She appeared in the soap opera *[Emmerdale](:Emmerdale)* as [Jean Hope](:Jean_Hope) in 2006, and her film appearances include *[Under Milk Wood](:Under_Milk_Wood_%281972_film%29)* (1972); *[No Sex Please, We're British](:No_Sex_Please%2C_We%27re_British_%28film%29)* (1973); *[The Land That Time Forgot](:The_Land_That_Time_Forgot_%281975_film%29)* (1974); *[The Uncanny](:The_Uncanny_%28film%29)* (1977); [Paul Verhoeven](:Paul_Verhoeven)'s *[Soldier of Orange](:Soldier_of_Orange)* (1977) and as [Lucy Westenra](:Lucy_Westenra) in *[Count Dracula](:Count_Dracula_%281977_film%29)* (1977). She has also had a substantial stage career.Tagged the \"British Bardot\" in the 1970s, she was described by [Clive Aslet](:Clive_Aslet) in *[The Daily Telegraph](:The_Daily_Telegraph)* as \"the face of the decade\"."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
