<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thomas_J._Geraghty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Thomas J. Geraghty (April 10, 1883 – June 5, 1945), was an American screenwriter. He wrote for 70 films between 1917 and 1939. During the 1930s he went to the United Kingdom, where he wrote a number of screenplays. He was born in Rushville, Indiana, and died in Hollywood, California. In April 1924, Geraghty was credited with coining the soon-to-be-popular vaudeville pun, \"The Thief of Badgags\"."@en .
