<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Munchies_(film)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Munchies*** is a 1987 [comedy horror](:Comedy_horror) film starring [Harvey Korman](:Harvey_Korman), Charlie Stratton, and [Nadine Van der Velde](:Nadine_Van_der_Velde). Directed by [Tina Hirsch](:Tina_Hirsch), the film editor for *[Gremlins](:Gremlins)*, the film features a similar plotline."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Roja_Selvamani> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Roja Selvamani** (born **Sri Latha Reddy**; 17 November 1972), also known as **R. K. Roja** or **Lady Roja Selvamani**, is an Indian politician and former actress. She is serving as the current Minister for Tourism, Culture and Youth Advancement of [Andhra Pradesh](:Andhra_Pradesh). She was a leading actress in [Telugu](:Telugu_language) and [Tamil](:Tamil_language) films from 1991 to 2002. She has also acted in a few [Kannada](:Kannada) and [Malayalam](:Malayalam)-language films. She won three [Nandi Awards](:Nandi_Awards) and one [Tamil Nadu State Film Award](:Tamil_Nadu_State_Film_Award).Roja began her political career in 1998 from the [Telugu Desam Party](:Telugu_Desam_Party) and aligns with the [YSR Congress Party](:YSR_Congress_Party) since 2011. She was elected as an [MLA](:MLA_%28India%29) from [Nagari](:Nagari_%28Assembly_constituency%29) in [Andhra Pradesh](:Andhra_Pradesh) twice in the [2014](:2014_Andhra_Pradesh_Legislative_Assembly_election) and [2019](:2019_Andhra_Pradesh_Legislative_Assembly_election). She also serves as the YSR Congress Party's state women president. Between 2019 and 2021, Roja served as the chairperson of [APIIC](:Andhra_Pradesh_Industrial_Infrastructure_Corporation) [Andhra Pradesh](:Andhra_pradesh). In 2022, Roja announced she would be leaving the film industry to focus more on her political career as a politician. She also announced that she will no longer be acting in any films. Roja is married to Tamil film director [R. K. Selvamani](:R%2E_K%2E_Selvamani)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
