<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Edward_Furlong> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Edward Walter Furlong** (born August 2, 1977) is an American actor. He won [Saturn](:Saturn_Award_for_Best_Performance_by_a_Younger_Actor) and [MTV Movie Awards](:MTV_Movie_Award_for_Best_Breakthrough_Performance) for his breakthrough performance at age 13 as [John Connor](:John_Connor) in [James Cameron](:James_Cameron)'s *[Terminator 2: Judgment Day](:Terminator_2%3A_Judgment_Day)*; which was followed by a mini-sequel, short attraction film *[T2-3D: Battle Across Time](:T2-3D%3A_Battle_Across_Time)* co-directed and co-written by Cameron with the same main cast. In 1992, he gave an [Independent Spirit Award](:Independent_Spirit_Awards)-nominated turn opposite [Jeff Bridges](:Jeff_Bridges) in *[American Heart](:American_Heart_%28film%29)*, and earned a second [Saturn Award](:Saturn_Award_for_Best_Performance_by_a_Younger_Actor) nomination for his work in *[Pet Sematary Two](:Pet_Sematary_Two)*. He won a [Young Artist Award](:Young_Artist_Award) for his performance alongside [Kathy Bates](:Kathy_Bates) in *[A Home of Our Own](:A_Home_of_Our_Own)* (1993) and appeared in *[Before and After](:Before_and_After_%28film%29)* (1996) with [Meryl Streep](:Meryl_Streep) and [Liam Neeson](:Liam_Neeson). Furlong received acclaim for his starring roles in the 1998 motion pictures *[Pecker](:Pecker_%28film%29)*, co-starring [Christina Ricci](:Christina_Ricci), and *[American History X](:American_History_X)*, co-starring [Edward Norton](:Edward_Norton). He had significant roles in the comedy *[Detroit Rock City](:Detroit_Rock_City_%28film%29)* (1999) and the crime drama *[Animal Factory](:Animal_Factory)* (2000)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
