<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rik_Mayall> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Richard Michael Mayall (7 March 1958 – 9 June 2014) was an English actor, stand-up comedian and writer. He formed a close partnership with Ade Edmondson while they were students at Manchester University and was a pioneer of alternative comedy in the 1980s. Mayall died suddenly at his home in London on 9 June 2014 at the age of 56. BBC Television director Danny Cohen praised him as a \"truly brilliant\" comedian with a unique stage presence, whose \"fireball creativity\" and approach to sitcom had inspired a generation of comedy stars."@en .
