<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rik_Mayall> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Richard Michael Mayall** (7 March 1958 – 9 June 2014) was an English actor, stand-up comedian and writer. He formed a close partnership with [Ade Edmondson](:Ade_Edmondson) while they were students at [Manchester University](:Victoria_University_of_Manchester) and was a pioneer of [alternative comedy](:Alternative_comedy) in the 1980s.Mayall starred in numerous successful comedy series throughout his career, including *[The Young Ones](:The_Young_Ones_%28TV_series%29)*, *[The Comic Strip Presents...](:The_Comic_Strip)*, *[Blackadder](:Blackadder)*, *[Filthy Rich & Catflap](:Filthy_Rich_%26_Catflap)*, *[The New Statesman](:The_New_Statesman_%281987_TV_series%29)*, *[Bottom](:Bottom_%28TV_series%29)* and *[Believe Nothing](:Believe_Nothing)*. Mayall also starred in the comedy films *[Drop Dead Fred](:Drop_Dead_Fred)* and *[Guest House Paradiso](:Guest_House_Paradiso)*; he won a [Primetime Emmy Award](:Primetime_Emmy_Award_for_Outstanding_Voice-Over_Performance) for his voice-over work in *[The Willows in Winter](:The_Wind_in_the_Willows_%281995_film)#Sequel)*. His comedic style was described as energetic \"[post-punk](:Post-punk)\".Mayall died suddenly at his home in London on 9 June 2014 at the age of 56. [BBC Television](:BBC_Television) director [Danny Cohen](:Danny_Cohen_%28television_executive%29) praised him as a \"truly brilliant\" comedian with a unique stage presence, whose \"fireball creativity\" and approach to sitcom had inspired a generation of comedy stars."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
