<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gaumont_Film_Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Gaumont Film Company (/ˈɡoʊmɒ̃/, French: [ɡomɔ̃]), often shortened to Gaumont, is a French major film studio headquartered in Neuilly-sur-Seine, France. Founded by the engineer-turned-inventor Léon Gaumont (1864–1946) in 1895, it is the oldest extant film company in the world, established before other studios such as Pathé (founded in 1896), Titanus (1904), Nordisk Film (1906), Universal, Paramount and Nikkatsu (founded in 1912). Gaumont is run by Nicolas Seydoux (President), Sidonie Dumas (General Director) and Christophe Riandee (Deputy General Director)."@en .
