<http://dbpedia.org/resource/ZaSu_Pitts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Zasu Pitts** (; January 3, 1894 – June 7, 1963) was an American actress who starred in many [silent](:Silent_film) [dramas](:Drama_film), including [Erich von Stroheim](:Erich_von_Stroheim)'s epic 1924 silent film *[Greed](:Greed_%281924_film%29)*, and comedies, transitioning successfully to mostly comedy films with the advent of [sound films](:Sound_film). She also appeared on numerous radio shows. Her career as an entertainer spanned nearly 50 years, and she was awarded a star on the [Hollywood Walk of Fame](:Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame) in 1960.Her parents named her \"ZaSu\" as an amalgamation of the two maiden aunts she had been named for."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
