<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kyle_Chandler> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Kyle Martin Chandler** (born September 17, 1965) is an American actor. Making his screen acting debut in a 1988 [television film](:Television_film), *[Quiet Victory: The Charlie Wedemeyer Story](:Quiet_Victory%3A_The_Charlie_Wedemeyer_Story)*, Chandler's first regular television role was in the [ABC](:American_Broadcasting_Company) [drama](:Drama) *[Homefront](:Homefront_%28U%2ES%2E_TV_series%29)* (1991–93). This was followed by the lead role of [Gary Hobson](:List_of_Early_Edition_characters%23Gary_Hobson) in the [CBS](:CBS) series *[Early Edition](:Early_Edition)* (1996–2000), for which he won a [Saturn Award for Best Actor on Television](:Saturn_Award_for_Best_Actor_on_Television). His other television roles include the [sitcom](:Situation_comedy) *[What About Joan?](:What_About_Joan%3F)* (2001) and the [legal drama](:Legal_drama) *[The Lyon's Den](:The_Lyon%27s_Den)* (2003), both short-lived, and a well-received guest appearance on the [medical drama](:Medical_drama) *[Grey's Anatomy](:Grey%27s_Anatomy)*, for which Chandler received his first [Primetime Emmy Award](:Primetime_Emmy_Award) nomination.Chandler received widespread critical acclaim for his performance as [Eric Taylor](:Eric_Taylor_%28Friday_Night_Lights%29) in *[Friday Night Lights](:Friday_Night_Lights_%28TV_series%29)* (2006–11); he received numerous award nominations for his portrayal of the character and won the [Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Lead Actor in a Drama Series](:Primetime_Emmy_Award_for_Outstanding_Lead_Actor_in_a_Drama_Series) in 2011 for his performance in the show's final season. Chandler's film work has included notable supporting roles in *[King Kong](:King_Kong_%282005_film%29)* (2005), *[The Day the Earth Stood Still](:The_Day_the_Earth_Stood_Still_%282008_film%29)* (2008), *[Super 8](:Super_8_%282011_film%29)* (2011), *[Argo](:Argo_%282012_film%29)*, *[Zero Dark Thirty](:Zero_Dark_Thirty)* (2012), *[The Wolf of Wall Street](:The_Wolf_of_Wall_Street_%282013_film%29)* (2013), *[Carol](:Carol_%28film%29)* (2015), *[Manchester by the Sea](:Manchester_by_the_Sea_%28film%29)* (2016), *[Game Night](:Game_Night_%28film%29)* and *[First Man](:First_Man_%28film%29)* (2018). He starred as Dr. Mark Russell in *[Godzilla: King of the Monsters](:Godzilla%3A_King_of_the_Monsters_%282019_film%29)* (2019), and *[Godzilla vs. Kong](:Godzilla_vs%2E_Kong)* (2021). Chandler's first starring role on television since the conclusion of *Friday Night Lights* was as Det. John Rayburn in the [Netflix](:Netflix) [thriller](:Thriller_film) *[Bloodline](:Bloodline_%28TV_series%29)* (2015–17), for which he received his fourth and fifth Primetime Emmy Award nominations. In 2021, he starred in the crime miniseries *[Mayor of Kingstown](:Mayor_of_Kingstown)*. In November 2022, he appeared as the character Peter in the [Netflix](:Netflix) film *[Slumberland](:Slumberland_%28film%29)*."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
