<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Terrence_Malick> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Terrence Frederick Malick (born November 30, 1943) is an American filmmaker. Malick began his career as part of the New Hollywood wave with the films Badlands (1973), about a murderous couple on the run in 1950s American Midwest, and Days of Heaven (1978), which detailed a love triangle between two laborers and a wealthy farmer during the First World War, before a lengthy hiatus."@en .
