<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eduardo_Serra> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Eduardo Martins Serra** (born 2 October 1943) is a Portuguese [cinematographer](:Cinematographer) who has spent most of his career working in European film productions, mostly in French, Portuguese and British films, with frequent collaborations with directors [Patrice Leconte](:Patrice_Leconte) and [Claude Chabrol](:Claude_Chabrol). Serra is best known for his work on the final two Harry Potter films, *[Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 1](:Harry_Potter_and_the_Deathly_Hallows_%E2%80%93_Part_1)* and *[Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 2](:Harry_Potter_and_the_Deathly_Hallows_%E2%80%93_Part_2)* .From 1960 to 1963, Serra studied engineering at Lisbon's [Instituto Superior Técnico](:Instituto_Superior_T%C3%A9cnico), but he had to leave the country after his involvement in students' protests against [Salazar](:Ant%C3%B3nio_de_Oliveira_Salazar)'s dictatorship. He settled in France, where he was accepted to [Vaugirard](:Louis_Lumi%C3%A8re_College) film school in Paris; he graduated in 1966. In 1970 he got his second degree from the [Paris-Sorbonne University](:Paris-Sorbonne_University), in Art History and Archeology.Serra has twice been nominated for the Academy Award for [Best Cinematography](:Academy_Award_for_Best_Cinematography). His first nomination was for his work on *[The Wings of the Dove](:The_Wings_of_the_Dove_%281997_film%29)* (1997), for which he also won a [BAFTA](:BAFTA_Award_for_Best_Cinematography). He received his second [Academy Award](:Academy_Awards) and [BAFTA](:British_Academy_Film_Awards) nominations for *[Girl with a Pearl Earring](:Girl_with_a_Pearl_Earring_%28film%29)*.In 2004, Serra received the *Ordem do Infante D. Henrique*, a civilian award presented for services to Portuguese culture, from President [Jorge Sampaio](:Jorge_Sampaio)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
