<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Anitha_Shaiq> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Anitha Shaiq**, often credited as Anitha. S is an Indian playback singer and music composer, living in [Mumbai](:Mumbai), India. She performs Indian [classical](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classical), [sufi](:Sufi), [Ghazal](:Ghazal), [folk](:Folk_music) and pop music, having sung in [Malayalam](:Malayalam), [Kannada](:Kannada), [Telugu](:Telugu_language), [Oriya](:Odia_language), [Punjabi](:Punjabi_language), and [Tamil](:Tamil_language) languages. In her 12 years in the film industry, she has recorded more than 100 songs for films. "^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
