<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Robert_Wiene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Robert Wiene (German: [ˈviːnə]; 27 April 1873 – 17 July 1938) was a film director of the silent era of German cinema. He is particularly known for directing the German silent film The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari and a succession of other expressionist films. Wiene also directed a variety of other films of varying styles and genres. Following the Nazi rise to power in Germany, Wiene, who was of Jewish descent, fled into exile."@en .
