<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kissed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Kissed*** is a 1996 Canadian romantic/erotic [drama film](:Drama_film) directed and co-written by [Lynne Stopkewich](:Lynne_Stopkewich), based on [Barbara Gowdy](:Barbara_Gowdy)'s short story \"We So Seldom Look on Love\". It premiered at the [Toronto International Film Festival](:Toronto_International_Film_Festival) on September 7, 1996.The film stars [Molly Parker](:Molly_Parker) as Sandra Larson, a young woman whose fixation on [death](:Death) leads her to study [embalming](:Embalming) at a mortuary school, where in turn she finds herself drawn toward feelings of [necrophilia](:Necrophilia). [Peter Outerbridge](:Peter_Outerbridge) also stars as Matt, a fellow student who develops romantic feelings for Sandra, and so must learn to accept her sexual proclivities."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
