<http://dbpedia.org/resource/The_New_World_(2005_film)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***The New World*** is a 2005 [historical](:Historical_drama) [romantic](:Romance_film) [drama film](:Drama_film) written and directed by [Terrence Malick](:Terrence_Malick), depicting the [founding of the Jamestown, Virginia, settlement](:History_of_the_Jamestown_Settlement_%281607%E2%80%931699%29) and inspired by the historical figures [Captain John Smith](:John_Smith_%28explorer%29), [Pocahontas](:Pocahontas) of the [Powhatan tribe](:Powhatan), and Englishman [John Rolfe](:John_Rolfe). It is the fourth feature film written and directed by Malick.The cast includes [Colin Farrell](:Colin_Farrell), [Q'orianka Kilcher](:Q%27orianka_Kilcher), [Christopher Plummer](:Christopher_Plummer), [Christian Bale](:Christian_Bale), [August Schellenberg](:August_Schellenberg), [Wes Studi](:Wes_Studi), [David Thewlis](:David_Thewlis), [Yorick van Wageningen](:Yorick_van_Wageningen) and [John Savage](:John_Savage_%28actor%29). The production team includes director of photography [Emmanuel Lubezki](:Emmanuel_Lubezki), producer [Sarah Green](:Sarah_Green_%28film_producer%29), production designer [Jack Fisk](:Jack_Fisk), costume designer [Jacqueline West](:Jacqueline_West), composer [James Horner](:James_Horner) and film editors [Richard Chew](:Richard_Chew), [Hank Corwin](:Hank_Corwin), [Saar Klein](:Saar_Klein) and Mark Yoshikawa.*The New World* was a box-office failure even though it received many award nominations for Lubezki's cinematography, Kilcher's acting and Horner's score. The film was initially met with an only mildly positive critical response, although several critics later ranked it as one of the best films of the decade."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
