<http://dbpedia.org/resource/ZaSu_Pitts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Zasu Pitts (/ˈseɪzuː ˈpɪts/; January 3, 1894 – June 7, 1963) was an American actress who starred in many silent dramas, including Erich von Stroheim's epic 1924 silent film Greed, and comedies, transitioning successfully to mostly comedy films with the advent of sound films. She also appeared on numerous radio shows. Her career as an entertainer spanned nearly 50 years, and she was awarded a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame in 1960. Her parents named her \"ZaSu\" as an amalgamation of the two maiden aunts she had been named for."@en .
