<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Roja_Selvamani> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Roja Selvamani (born Sri Latha Reddy; 17 November 1972), also known as R. K. Roja, is an Indian politician and former actress. She is serving as the current Minister for Tourism, Culture and Youth Advancement of Andhra Pradesh. She was a leading actress in Tamil and Telugu films from 1991 to 2002. She has also acted in a few Kannada and Malayalam-language films. She won three Nandi Awards and one Tamil Nadu State Film Award."@en .
